  "result": "Implemented `wire/codec.py`. All 6 tests pass:\n\n```\n6 passed in 0.02s\n```\n\n**Approach chosen: A, compact binary.** I picked it because `struct` round-trips every IEEE-754 double bit-exactly, including NaN, -0.0, and 1e300, which JSON only handles through non-standard extensions, and a fixed-width layout makes truncation detection a simple length check.\n\nThe format is a 13-byte header holding a `WIRE` magic, a version byte, the record count, and a CRC32 of the payload. Each record follows as 15 packed big-endian bytes. On decode, `CodecError` is raised for bad magic, unknown version, short or trailing data, and checksum mismatch. Beyond the test suite, I also confirmed a single flipped payload byte, empty input, trailing bytes, and a truncated header all raise `CodecError`.\n\nNothing is committed. The only new tracked-candidate file is `wire/codec.py`.",
